<p>When you create several sheets of data in applications such as Microsoft® 
 Excel® and want to print out all sheets using the same print settings, 
 you can apply the print settings of the first sheet to the rest. By using 
 this function, you need not to make print settings for the other sheets.</p>
<p><img alt="" class="help-img" height="179" loading="lazy" src="~/images/help/Bappli.gif" width="330"/> </p>
<ol>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Make the print 
 settings for the first of the four sheets of data.</p></li>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">These print 
 settings are applied to the remaining three sheets.</p></li>
</ol>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">To use this 
 function, log on as a member of the Administrators or Power Users group.</p></li>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Following print 
 settings are not applied to the remaining sheets;</p></li>
</ul>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<p class="Normal-indent"><span class="Term-Soft">Document Size:</span>, 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Orientation</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Custom 
 Paper Size</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Printable Area:</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Vector/Raster:</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Color/ Black 
 and White:</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">2 sided:</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Resolution:</span>, 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Use Application Zoom</span></p>
</div>
<ol>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-OS">Devices and Printers</span> 
 window, open the printer properties dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start="2">
<li><p>On the <span class="Term-Soft">Advanced Options</span> 
 tab, select the <span class="Term-Soft">Increase Auto-keep Settings for 
 Applications</span> check box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the 
 printer properties dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
